## Requirement ruling applied

The brief's output-directory condition conflicted with the required tracked
`exports/pit/.gitkeep` and its prescribed validation path.  Per the parent
agent's ruling, the CLI allows an existing output directory only when it is
empty or contains exactly `.gitkeep`; it still refuses existing generated or
temporary target files.

## Notes

The local Python environment lacked an HTML-table parser for `pandas.read_html`.
Installed `lxml` into that local environment solely to perform the requested
functional validation; no dependency-manifest file was changed.

## Fix Round 1

Addressed the Task 1 review findings:

- Redirect handling now requires every redirect target and the final response
  URL to remain HTTPS, on the original host, and retain the original numeric
  `oldid` revision identifier.
- The CLI now rejects every date window except exactly 2021-01-01 through
  2025-12-31 before it touches the output directory or network.
- Provenance now records SHA-256 values for `membership.csv`,
  `security_names.csv`, and `membership_spot_checks.json` after those files
  are atomically written.  The existing raw-source SHA-256 remains unchanged.
- `MembershipExport` copies `company_names` and every exclusion mapping into
  read-only mapping proxies, including for direct public construction.
- A pre-existing output directory is now accepted only when it contains
  exactly `.gitkeep`; an absent directory remains valid and is created only
  after successful acquisition and normalization.

Focused validation commands and output:

```text
python - (focused invariants)
focused invariant checks passed

python fetch_sp500_membership.py ... --start-date 2021-01-02
fetch_sp500_membership.py: error: membership window must be exactly
2021-01-01 through 2025-12-31

python fetch_sp500_membership.py ... --symbol-map-csv ... --output-dir exports/pit
event_count=679, symbol_count=591, first_effective_date=2021-01-01,
last_effective_date=2025-12-22

python - (verify emitted hashes and spot checks)
artifact hashes and spot checks verified

python -c "... PointInTimeUniverse.from_csv(...) ..."
679 505 503

python -m py_compile core/public_membership.py fetch_sp500_membership.py
git diff --check
```

The focused invariant script verifies final HTTP-downgrade and changed-`oldid`
redirect rejection, nonexact-date rejection, direct mutation rejection for
both immutable export mapping fields, and the exact `.gitkeep` pre-existing
directory policy.  The emitted manifest hashes were recomputed from the three
written files and matched exactly.

## Fix Round 2: point-in-time ticker identity

The pinned 2026 constituent snapshot labeled Marsh McLennan `MRSH`, although
the issuer's October 16, 2025 release says the NYSE ticker would change from
`MMC` to `MRSH` only in January 2026. The parser had applied reviewed mappings
to dated membership changes but not to the current-constituent snapshot, so the
future ticker leaked into the 2021 seed.

Reviewed mappings now project the snapshot and out-of-window change rows onto
the evaluation cutoff. Contiguous date ranges with different canonical tickers
also emit explicit same-company membership swaps. The tracked mapping source is
`config/pit_membership_symbol_map.csv`; its full rows, reasons, official URLs,
and SHA-256 are recorded in `membership_provenance.json`.

Corrected intervals:

- Before: `MRSH` was active 2021-01-01 through 2025-12-31. After: `MMC` is
  active for the full evaluation interval and `MRSH` is absent.
- Before: `DAY` was active beginning 2021-09-20. After: `CDAY` is active from
  2021-09-20 through 2024-01-31; `CDAY` exits and `DAY` enters on 2024-02-01.

Primary evidence:

- Marsh McLennan 3Q25 issuer release:
  `https://www.marshmclennan.com/web-assets/files-for-download/investors/2025/pdf-2025-marsh-mclennan-investors-3q-news-release.pdf`
- Dayforce Form 8-K:
  `https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1725057/000095017024009619/day-20240131.htm`

Functional regeneration results:

- raw source SHA-256 unchanged:
  `8940a97243ad30664b2d0e606e832fec13e6bf38c250b1c999cff8a94093e14d`
- reviewed map SHA-256:
  `a9781f0a2989dc0ec50e3ae3e512738f098ee4325018a062f4d0691ba2d78948`
- membership SHA-256:
  `23a3c5e09f266da1db29ce9c458dd994a07b763666b59309a87f79f88de06f56`
- security names SHA-256:
  `a943a681fb47fc239ad77cabfa87af9ebc87b8f75b0769fdf8d619f9af6d7ef3`
- 681 unique events, 592 union symbols, 505 members on 2021-01-01, and
  503 members on 2025-12-31; the CDAY/DAY swap preserves 503 active members.

Narrow regression checks passed (`3 passed`) and both Python modules compiled;
`git diff --check` passed. The generated artifact hashes were recomputed and
matched provenance.

### Follow-up identity audit

The tracked reviewed mapping previously contained only the broad CDAY-to-DAY
row; no other reviewed source rows existed. A read-only CIK comparison against
immutable Wikipedia revision `978246445` exposed additional snapshot identities
that need the same dated treatment before the bundle can be called fully ticker-
PIT: BLL/BALL, ABC/COR, ANTM/ELV, COG/CTRA, RE/EG, FB/META, FLT/CPAY,
PEAK/DOC, NLOK/GEN, PKI/RVTY, and WLTW/WTW. The pinned page also leaves Fiserv
as stale `FISV`, and the 2021 seed currently leaks `PSKY` across the historical
VIAC/PARA/PSKY chain. DISCA/DISCK/WBD is already represented by explicit index
change rows. The share-class cross-products GOOG/GOOGL and NWS/NWSA are not
ticker changes. These discovered rows were not silently guessed into this
narrow repair; each needs an official-source effective date and review.

## Fix Round 3: complete reviewed identity map

Completed the official-source identity audit and regenerated the functional
five-year export. The tracked map now contains 30 rows across 15 source chains:
the 27 newly reviewed rows plus the existing two DAY rows and one MRSH row.
Every source chain is required to cover 2021-01-01 through 2025-12-31 exactly;
both overlaps and calendar gaps fail before normalization.

Corrected identity intervals:

- `BALL`: BLL 2021-01-01 through 2022-05-09; BALL 2022-05-10 through 2025-12-31.
- `COR`: ABC 2021-01-01 through 2023-08-29; COR 2023-08-30 through 2025-12-31.
- `ELV`: ANTM 2021-01-01 through 2022-06-27; ELV 2022-06-28 through 2025-12-31.
- `CTRA`: COG 2021-01-01 through 2021-10-03; CTRA 2021-10-04 through 2025-12-31.
- `EG`: RE 2021-01-01 through 2023-07-09; EG 2023-07-10 through 2025-12-31.
- `META`: FB 2021-01-01 through 2022-06-08; META 2022-06-09 through 2025-12-31.
- `CPAY`: FLT 2021-01-01 through 2024-03-24; CPAY 2024-03-25 through 2025-12-31.
- `DOC`: PEAK 2021-01-01 through 2024-03-03; DOC 2024-03-04 through 2025-12-31.
- `GEN`: NLOK 2021-01-01 through 2022-11-07; GEN 2022-11-08 through 2025-12-31.
- `RVTY`: PKI 2021-01-01 through 2023-05-15; RVTY 2023-05-16 through 2025-12-31.
- `WTW`: WLTW 2021-01-01 through 2022-01-09; WTW 2022-01-10 through 2025-12-31.
- `FISV`: FISV 2021-01-01 through 2023-06-06; FI 2023-06-07 through 2025-12-31.
- `PSKY`: VIAC 2021-01-01 through 2022-02-16; PARA 2022-02-17 through 2025-08-06; PSKY 2025-08-07 through 2025-12-31.
- `DAY`: CDAY 2021-01-01 through 2024-01-31; DAY 2024-02-01 through 2025-12-31.
- `MRSH`: MMC for the complete 2021-01-01 through 2025-12-31 evaluation window.

The PSKY rows and their emitted provenance explicitly classify PARA-to-PSKY as
a successor-issuer transaction. They are an index-membership identity chain
only and do not assert entity, raw-price, or position continuity. The CTRA and
DOC reasons likewise preserve the reviewed accounting/predecessor boundaries.
Every row retains its full primary issuer or SEC evidence URL.

The public `fetch_membership` API and CLI now default to the tracked reviewed
map while retaining a regular-file/non-symlink explicit path override. The map
loader reads the file once, parses those exact bytes, and carries their digest
to provenance, eliminating the prior parse/hash TOCTOU. Snapshot company names
are propagated to every reviewed historical ticker identity, so every emitted
membership symbol has a security-name row.

Functional regeneration from immutable revision `1347775889` produced:

- 709 unique and deterministically sorted events over 606 union symbols.
- 505 active members on 2021-01-01 and 503 on 2025-12-31.
- 876 security-name rows with zero emitted membership symbols missing a name.
- All 15 in-window identity boundaries represented by same-day removal/addition pairs.
- All five official S&P spot checks matched and exclusions remained empty.

